          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: incomplete because cost-event evidence is unavailable\n\nI verified the relevant work order and the exact Pending Close cutoff, but **cannot determine whether a late-created event occurred** from the records available under analyst access.\n\n| Requested item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine, DeKoven — Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 / PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not verifiable from accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe timestamp above is reproduced exactly; the source does not specify a timezone.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied **Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B** policy, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page **233** / printed page **225**, states that:\n\n- New transactions created after Pending Close that relate to the current or an earlier period **will not be staged or processed** until the period is closed or reopened.\n- Transactions entered before Pending Close continue to be processed.\n- **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments** continue to be processed despite Pending Close.\n\nConsequently, an ordinary new manufacturing transaction created after the cutoff should be held from staging/processing. Assessing this event’s recorded status requires its actual creation time, event type, and status.\n\n### Evidence limitation and delivery\n\nThe accessible task records contain work orders, cost periods, and the policy excerpt, but **no cost-event rows**. Supporting records remain unstaged and restricted to the records-custodian role; no authorized extract was provided after the staging requests. This is an evidence gap—not proof that no late event occurred.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial report was submitted with status **`needs_evidence`** and saved with provenance at:\n\n`/cache/work/worker_c2eb21db1ca9/audit-report.json`",
